WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.331 --> 00:00:01.323
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.323 --> 00:00:04.811
(audience applauding)

00:00:04.811 --> 00:00:05.922
- (indistinct).

00:00:05.922 --> 00:00:08.250
Oh, look, live people.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.500
- I know we're here, I
know, it's not virtual.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.735
You're here in person.

00:00:11.735 --> 00:00:12.568
- I know.
- [Kelly] Basically,

00:00:12.568 --> 00:00:13.401
I love it.

00:00:13.401 --> 00:00:14.234
It's nice to see you

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:15.067
- [Tim] Nice to see you.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.560
- I know, I'm freaking
out about the Santa Claus

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:17.460
and we're gonna get to it.(chuckles)

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.160
But I hear that you love
changing the design of rooms

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.344
when you go places, so--

00:00:21.344 --> 00:00:23.125
- [Tim] That was a weird
story your people came up with

00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:23.958
I've been--
- [Kelly] So,

00:00:23.958 --> 00:00:24.791
you've never done that.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:25.624
- I do it all the time.

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:26.457
- [Kelly] Okay!

00:00:26.457 --> 00:00:29.009
We didn't come up with it.
- But I'd say...

00:00:29.009 --> 00:00:29.842
Somebody asked me a question.

00:00:29.842 --> 00:00:31.784
It'd be sometimes like I
walk into somebody's room

00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:33.067
and while we're talking, I'd go,

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:35.190
"It's just great that this...

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.360
That."
- Oh.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.700
- Constantly, I'm on the road a lot.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.440
Besides doing movies and TV,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.920
I do Vegas and travel
and I look at those...

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.080
Get out of a hotel every floor,

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.297
there's two chairs at a table.

00:00:48.297 --> 00:00:49.130
- Yes.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:49.963
- And you get off the elevator.

00:00:49.963 --> 00:00:50.796
- Yeah.

00:00:50.796 --> 00:00:51.750
- Is anybody so tired in the elevator?

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.260
They get out and they go,
"Thank God there's a chair.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:54.093
(audience laughs)

00:00:54.093 --> 00:00:54.990
I could sit,"

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.732
but I'm genuinely I've always
moved the flower arrangement

00:00:58.732 --> 00:01:00.450
a little to the left there's a
statue or horse or something.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:01.440
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And I think to myself,

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.127
there's somebody in the
security camera goes,

00:01:03.127 --> 00:01:04.710
"What is that tool boy doing? (laughs)

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.770
Why does he get off every day
and move this stuff around?"

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.420
And it's an ADD thing.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.591
- [Kelly] Do you...

00:01:10.591 --> 00:01:11.424
I was like...

00:01:11.424 --> 00:01:13.050
I'm kinda like that, especially
with pictures on the wall.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:13.883
- Yes.

00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:15.317
- I can't think of anything else,

00:01:15.317 --> 00:01:16.350
if I see it.
- [Tim] Well, I do...

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.893
My mother who is now...

00:01:17.893 --> 00:01:20.910
We put her into a "condo"
is I could tell her,

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.320
her house all, she's short. (laughs)

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.410
So, all the pictures are real struc--

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:26.980
- Is that assisted living?

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:27.813
Is that what it is, kind of a?

00:01:27.813 --> 00:01:28.950
- Oh, it's such a long story.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.090
So it's...

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:30.981
Which is--

00:01:30.981 --> 00:01:31.814
- I just can't believe that you
called it a condo.(chuckles)

00:01:31.814 --> 00:01:34.777
- The only way I could get
her in it is they said,

00:01:34.777 --> 00:01:36.660
"Hey think of it as a condo."
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.197
- And her whole demeanor says,

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.260
"Oh like in Florida or something?"

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.120
Yeah, that would be it.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.260
- Except it's in mid-Michigan,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:46.230
but yeah, consider it a condo in Florida.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:48.000
- [Kelly] But people take
care of you, that's nice.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.500
They play games, they do stuff?

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:50.333
- Yeah.

00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.166
- [Kelly] Yeah?
- Uh-huh.

00:01:51.166 --> 00:01:51.999
- [Kelly] Do you feel like it's your turn

00:01:51.999 --> 00:01:53.400
to take care of your mama now?

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.550
- Well, nobody trains
you how to be a parent,

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:57.810
and certainly nobody trains you

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.010
how to be a parent to your parent.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:01:59.970
And it's a--
- Yeah.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.260
- Luckily there's nine of us

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.826
and we're able to move all of
us are doing it, but it's--

00:02:03.826 --> 00:02:05.790
- [Kelly] I forget how many brothers

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.080
or siblings you have, wow!

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.270
- Yeah, I'm lucky because I
have a lot of good friends

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.070
that are taking care of
their parents on their own.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.590
And it's so much.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:14.880
- If you're doing it or you see it,

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:16.630
it's really difficult 'cause--

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:18.630
- Well, it's time consuming
if you also have a job

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:20.148
and you also have a family, it's--

00:02:20.148 --> 00:02:21.150
- [Tim] And they can be...

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.792
My mother once looked at me.

00:02:22.792 --> 00:02:25.244
I've had a good relationship with my mom,

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:27.330
I've been in a lot of trouble in my life.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.120
And so, she and I have
come to an understanding

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.177
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:31.177 --> 00:02:32.400
- That none of my bad
behavior was her problem

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.990
if I made my own bad decisions.

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:34.823
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:34.823 --> 00:02:35.656
- And I've helped her through this.

00:02:35.656 --> 00:02:36.930
But she was...

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:38.880
I've been like a friend of hers. (laughs)

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.180
Because I listened to
everything she has to say

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:41.850
and I don't give her any advice.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:42.690
And so--
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:44.640
- She's mean right now at
all my brothers. (chuckles)

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.320
And she finally got mean to me one day...

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.020
I was telling her, "You can't do this."

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.300
She didn't make any sense,
she's making weird sentences.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.133
And I said, I don't understand.

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:53.017
"You're calling me a liar."

00:02:53.017 --> 00:02:53.910
"No, I didn't call you a liar,

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:56.430
but the first part of that
sentence did not match

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:57.330
the last part."

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:58.380
She goes, "You know what?

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.481
Why don't you go to lunch
and don't hurry back?"

00:03:00.481 --> 00:03:03.024
(laughing)

00:03:03.024 --> 00:03:05.603
I laughed at first, I went,
"Aha, are you serious?

00:03:05.603 --> 00:03:07.260
Did you just say that to me?"

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:11.220
And that she doesn't know
how to shut things off.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.053
And I said,

00:03:12.053 --> 00:03:13.050
it's a true talent.
- Yeah, oh my mom,

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:16.410
she'll hate me for
this, she has no filter.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:19.290
Do not ask my mom for the truth. (laughs)

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.880
'Cause she will serve it up on a platter

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:21.810
and be like, "You asked".

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:23.010
- But you're not asking for it.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.171
- Yeah.
- That's what I'm saying--

00:03:24.171 --> 00:03:25.380
- No, no. She does that too.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:26.580
You don't even have to ask.
- Yeah.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.050
- [Kelly] Yeah, she does that too.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:31.110
Anyway, but you talked about
your design compulsion.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.060
So who wins at your house?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.230
Like if you and your wife are like,

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.150
you want something somewhere and she...

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:36.983
Who goes--
- Luckily,

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.730
my wife and I are both neat nicks.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.530
I mean, I'm a little bit
more of a neat nick than her

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.930
but it's always one item in the house

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:44.790
that's passive aggressive fighting.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.320
And it happens to be a lamp, we have that.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.110
I'll come in, I go, "Why
is that lamp over there?"

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:51.810
And I'll go in and it's
literally six inches to the left.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:52.980
I go like this,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.297
and I know she's probably coming
into the bedroom she goes,

00:03:55.297 --> 00:03:57.090
"Why is that lamp like that?" (laughs)

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.740
And this is going on for years,

00:03:58.740 --> 00:03:59.970
where every time I come back in,

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:01.740
that lamp is back over there, "Who's?"

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.744
And I know who's putting it back there.

00:04:03.744 --> 00:04:04.808
(laughing)

00:04:04.808 --> 00:04:05.641
I do that--
- Kelly] When you say it

00:04:05.641 --> 00:04:07.645
passive aggressively--
- [Tim] I make it yeah.

00:04:07.645 --> 00:04:09.079
- "Who keeps doing this?"
- "Who keeps doing that,

00:04:09.079 --> 00:04:11.010
moving the lamp to the left?"

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:13.020
- Are you in the middle
guy, or an off center?

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.537
'Cause I'm off center--
- Off center

00:04:14.537 --> 00:04:15.450
is called asymmetrical design.

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.000
I went to design school and I
explained this to my family.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.003
- [Kelly] Oh you did?
- Yes.

00:04:19.003 --> 00:04:20.615
- I didn't actually know that.

00:04:20.615 --> 00:04:21.448
- Yeah, I love design.
- Oh!

00:04:21.448 --> 00:04:22.410
- I wanted to be interior designer.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:23.970
Landscape designer really like that,

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:25.650
but product design is really nice.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:26.703
- [Kelly] I love that too.
- I love it.

00:04:26.703 --> 00:04:28.650
- [Kelly] I've like read books on Olmsted

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.540
like I'm a nerd about landscape.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.770
He did Central Park, he
did all these parks--

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.300
- [Tim] Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Started like,

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.160
I'm a nerd about stuff like
that, I think it's cool.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.690
- Well the guy, the guy that I like was a

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:38.910
Brooks Stevens, I believe
that's his name, but some...

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:40.140
The guy that changed the washing machines

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:42.150
from a gray machine in the basement.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:45.090
He said, "Why don't we make
them white with a window in it

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:45.927
so you can see the wash?"
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:45.927 --> 00:04:48.180
- And he changed the whole zeitgeist

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.013
of washing machines

00:04:49.013 --> 00:04:50.391
for (indistinct)--
- Design is important,

00:04:50.391 --> 00:04:51.224
I agree.
- [Tim] I love it,

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:52.057
I love it, I love it.

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:53.310
- My also is more with like Central Park,

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.540
I like the landscaping stuff.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.370
I like indoors as well, like interiors,

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.200
but I think it's just beautiful
what you can do with nature

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.680
and make it, just accent it.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.110
- Yeah, product design is my...

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:02.609
I love product design.

00:05:02.609 --> 00:05:03.442
- [Kelly] Yeah?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:03.442 --> 00:05:04.275
- [Kelly] That's cool,

00:05:04.275 --> 00:05:05.280
I didn't know this about
you, okay. (applauding)

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.425
I mentioned Vegas earlier,
so do you like doing Vegas?

00:05:09.425 --> 00:05:13.428
- Yeah, Vegas is a peculiar place because

00:05:13.428 --> 00:05:16.350
when I do concerts, people
pay tickets to come see me.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.220
In Vegas--
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:18.700
- Sometimes it's the last
thing that on their mind

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:20.566
"Well I guess I got to
go to that comedian."

00:05:20.566 --> 00:05:22.134
(laughing)

00:05:22.134 --> 00:05:23.070
- It's like a corporate event.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:24.434
- It's a corporate...

00:05:24.434 --> 00:05:25.860
Well, sometimes it's free
tickets, sometimes it's giveaways.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:28.770
And often you get people that
just lost a lot of money.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.930
- [Kelly] Yeah, so they're excited.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:31.830
- [Tim] Yeah, they're really,
yeah, that's just great.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.570
Or the real drunks that
make a lot of money

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:34.710
at the ATM machine.

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:35.981
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:35.981 --> 00:05:36.814
- "Oh I keep winning,
this is great. (laughs)

00:05:36.814 --> 00:05:37.647
I just went through these numbers

00:05:37.647 --> 00:05:38.977
and I just keep getting money."

00:05:38.977 --> 00:05:39.930
- "It gives me money."

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:40.967
Oh my God,

00:05:40.967 --> 00:05:42.332
(chuckles) I'm gonna do
that when I lose there.

00:05:42.332 --> 00:05:43.297
(laughing)

00:05:43.297 --> 00:05:44.580
Yeah, so you posted an
iconic photo recently,

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:46.170
I love this photo.
- [Tim] Yeah.

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:48.852
Look at how many amazing
people are in this photo,

00:05:48.852 --> 00:05:50.465
(applauding) all of y'all.

00:05:50.465 --> 00:05:51.870
(applauding)

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.910
I mean, that's an iconic photo man.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.710
- Yeah.
- So what comes to mind

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.135
when you see a photo like this?

00:05:57.135 --> 00:05:58.890
- Well, first my dear friend
has passed away, Bob Saget,

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.960
who just recently, who I loved dearly.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.710
And that picture though is at that time,

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:06.300
Robin (indistinct) again passed away.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.370
You can't keep up with him.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:09.510
I'm really good off the cup.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.120
I'm not as probably the
fastest guy on the planet,

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.040
mentally, as Marty Short.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.200
That, if you go to a
party with Marty Short,

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.580
you're sick to your stomach laughing.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:18.810
So you have to leave.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.390
- He won't shut up.
- Yeah.(laughs)

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:22.290
- As I said, I've done
couple movies with him.

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:24.307
A director has never ever told Marty Short

00:06:24.307 --> 00:06:27.063
"Could you go bigger?" (laughing)

00:06:27.063 --> 00:06:27.896
- You Just...

00:06:27.896 --> 00:06:30.570
You've never said, he makes
noise getting out of a seat.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:31.805
It's, "Oh!"
- Very good.

00:06:31.805 --> 00:06:33.007
(laughing)

00:06:33.007 --> 00:06:34.507
"Marty, you're just
getting out of a chair."

00:06:34.507 --> 00:06:35.803
"Oh!"

00:06:35.803 --> 00:06:37.560
- There's comedy we had everywhere.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:39.275
- [Tim] Everywhere.

00:06:39.275 --> 00:06:41.922
Well that Rodney in that
pictures trying to say something.

00:06:41.922 --> 00:06:44.130
He's, "Oh, 'mumbles'."

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.200
He's waiting for Robin
to finish the sentence.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.033
- Yeah.

00:06:47.033 --> 00:06:48.007
- And he was getting really frustrated.

00:06:48.007 --> 00:06:51.927
"I had (indistinct), yeah,
I thought this years ago."

00:06:51.927 --> 00:06:53.190
And I'm laughing because

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:54.870
Rodney's gonna have a
nervous breakdown.(laughs)

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:56.850
Saget was going, "Have you
seen the buffet?"(laughing)

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:58.599
He just wanted to eat something.

00:06:58.599 --> 00:07:00.727
And Lovitz's sitting in the back going,

00:07:00.727 --> 00:07:02.670
"I'm Jon Lovitz, I'm actually Jon Lovitz.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.320
I will say they should." (laughs)

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:07.050
He was the most amazing
to be around those comics.

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:09.000
But once again, Williams is...

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.580
We went to a vacation in Mexico.

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:14.107
He came out of a spa, he and
his wife and my wife and I,

00:07:14.107 --> 00:07:15.150
"Hey, we're going in Robin."

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:18.750
And Robin and I did a
probably a 20 minute bit fest.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.127
We just doing all this acting and acting.

00:07:20.127 --> 00:07:21.660
And my wife was going to his wife...

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.760
They were saying hello to each other.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.695
We walk away and my wife goes,
"What just happened there?"

00:07:26.695 --> 00:07:27.528
(laughs)

00:07:27.528 --> 00:07:30.450
I said, "Robin got a new
car, his older boy having..."

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.107
I went through all the stuff, she goes,

00:07:32.107 --> 00:07:33.510
"Somehow in the middle of that

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:35.400
you got all that information?" (laughs)

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.980
I said, "Well, comics do bits, or rifts,

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:40.440
and in there I hear what
they're actually saying."

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.120
- [Kelly] I love that, and
other people are confused,

